# Plugin Guide and product nouns

## Plugin Guide is one roster

`plugins/plugin-guide/src/surfaces.ts` `SURFACE_GROUPS` is the source of truth for plugin surfaces.

When you add, rename, or regroup a surface, update all three in the same change:

1. The in-app Plugin Guide card (`surfaces.ts` + wireframe mark)
2. `docs/extensions-sdk-reference.md` (a `### {group.title}` heading and a `` `{id}` `` bullet)
3. `website/lib/plugin-guide/` via `node website/scripts/sync-plugin-guide.mjs` (also a website `predev` / `prebuild` hook)

Do not hand-edit `website/lib/plugin-guide/` — it is a generated copy of the ProductMap sources and `plugin-guide.css`. Edit `plugins/plugin-guide/`, then run the sync. The copy drops `.js` from relative imports so Next can resolve the TypeScript files.

`plugins/plugin-guide/src/api-sync.test.ts` fails if any copy is missing. Run that test after Plugin Guide or public plugin-doc edits. `website/content/docs/` is generated by `website/scripts/sync-docs.mjs` — edit `docs/*.md`, not the synced copy.

## Projects, not Workspaces

User-facing copy says **Project** (sidebar, Organize menu, project rail, project statusbar, project tab).

Keep these as API/path identifiers, and explain them in product language:

- `placement: "workspace"` → Projects header with no project selected (`projectId: null`)
- `--source workspace` / `openWorkspaceFile` → a file in the project directory vs thread storage
- `~/.zcc/personal-workspaces/` → personal scratch environment folder

Do not call the third column or the project rail a "workspace" in docs or Plugin Guide copy.
